An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Most items have an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md
(a few record instead in a design doc or a differently-named plan,
named in the item), and the planning/implementation/review process (who
plans, who implements, who reviews, which gates run) is
docs/plans/README.md.
No item is deferred to post-release, and gate labels (decision-gated,
consumer-gated) rank priority rather than block work (VD 2026-07-17).
Standing rule (VD 2026-08-06): gate an item IF we cannot think of
anything valuable it might enable - that failure, not the absence of
a caller today, is the only licensed gating fact. "consumer-gated"
below reads accordingly, and the gate lifts the moment a valuable
enabled model or use comes to mind. An existing consumer is
sufficient evidence of value, never necessary.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

Standing discipline (from the 2026-08-07 census): verify an entry's
status claims against git and live code before scoping from it;
re-run a full census before release.

A "door" below means a recorded, undecided question, not a task; an
entry can be otherwise closed and still list open doors.

items
  augmentation-helpers: dbartsDrawLatents and dbartsWorkingResponse
    are shipped (docs/plans/adoption-slate.md). Open: the valgrind leg
    never ran (darwin/arm64, valgrind.yaml unregistered off bartcore)
    - rides the first nightly after bartcore reaches main; per-push CI
    sanitizers cover the tinytest file under instrumented R meanwhile.
  bcf-baseline-cross-host: CLOSED (docs/plans/bcf-cross-host.md;
    prerc-surface-freeze.md D7). Remaining: the RC-tip re-record refresh.
  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: OPTIONAL research door (docs/plans/bcf-sigma-
    residual.md sec 4 item 2; no separate plan doc). Open: the EXTREME
    tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the prior) is frozen-structure mixing
    that no amount of burn fixes; a principled remedy would target
    tree-structure mixing at high SNR (tempered early sweeps,
    restart-style grow proposals). Low priority - the regime only
    arises with a stale build scale swapped against a new response
    inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse updateScale=FALSE).
    research-open, decision-gated.
  binary-kforest-k1-reachability: K = 1 as a SHIPPED multi-forest
    configuration - one varying-coefficient forest with no prognostic
    partner, which is VCBART's shape (D4 of docs/design/model-space-
    survey.md). Today it is a designed refusal (spec.R, added by
    docs/plans/archive/binary-kforest-prior-default.md). Priced live rather than
    inherited: the engine already takes it - drawGlue dispatches
    K != 2 to the general drawAmplitudes, synthesizeIndicatorBasis is
    gated on numForests_ > 1, shippedShape() is simply false at K = 1,
    and createBCFSampler imposes no count floor - so this is a bridge
    (applyAmplitudeSpec's Rf_xlength < 2) plus R change with tests,
    NOT engine work. Gated on ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE: a new shipped
    configuration owes its own, which is why that plan refused rather
    than opened it.
  correlated-outcomes: multivariate/SUR outcomes SHIPPED as mvbart()
    in stan4bart with zero dbarts code (docs/design/correlated-
    outcomes.md). Open: AR-1 / serially-correlated errors
    (longitudinal, panel, ITS, DiD) compose today via a latent
    AR-state + nugget in the outer sampler (the rbart_vi pattern),
    with EXACT pure-AR-1 errors a deferred ENGINE door (banded
    residual precision + cross-leaf GLS leaf updates break per-leaf
    independence). causal-motivated, decision-gated.
  equivalence-harness-statistical-mode: CLOSED - the multinomial half at
    the level-centering fix (docs/plans/archive/multinomial-level-centering.md),
    the bcf half with cross-host mode LANDED 3f532af2 (docs/plans/bcf-cross-host.md).
    Remaining, both doors open at docs/plans/bcf-cross-host.md: the
    RC-tip re-record refresh (not a prerequisite - the current
    .rds already suffices), and a post-RC seeds-axis re-record
    replacing the single-chain autocorrelated draws with independent
    per-scenario seeds.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost) and low-rank kernels. Value gate lifted by the
    model-space survey: GP-leaf BART as a surrogate for sequential
    design of computer experiments (arXiv 1203.1078), where a FIXED
    lengthscale asks the user to know the thing they are estimating;
    low-rank kernels serve the standing n >= 1e5 fact. decision-gated
    on cost, no longer on value.
  gpu-bart: backend-seam design waits on frontier items 4-5
    (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes); memo and falsifiers in
    docs/design/gpu-bart.md and parallel-bart-frontier.md.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). Value gate lifted:
    clustered / multi-site causal survival (riAFTBART's shape) plus
    grouped discrete-time hazard, which docs/design/survival.md sec 6
    calls feasible by construction with only surface work left. Pairs
    with sparse-extensions' rbart_vi-on-sparse half. decision-gated.
  grow-from-root: frontier 3.1's exact informed-proposal use of the
    shared scan.
  integer-predictor-storage: dense-INTEGER storage in the
    PredictorSource view. A memory win, not speed; integer -> double
    is exact in range so this change MUST be trio-bitwise. Split out of
    typed-ingestion at its close. consumer-gated.
  interaction-constraints: CLOSED (docs/design/interaction-constraints.md,
    docs/plans/archive/interaction-constraints.md,
    docs/plans/archive/interaction-constraints-p4.md).
    Remaining doors: formal heredity (ensemble lattice prior) - value
    gate lifted, enabling functional-ANOVA BART (arXiv 2509.03317),
    for which dbarts already ships the hard-constraint half; soft
    path-dependent penalties, gate STANDS - no model surfaced. Formal
    heredity is scheduled first post-1.0 (VD 2026-08-26), not pre-RC.
  monotone-leaf-branch-fill: CLOSED, not adopted; benched 2026-08-26, no
    effect (within noise; fillBottom 0.18% of monotone run). Bitwise;
    open door: coneProbability's quadrature, an alternative not yet
    benched; see review-2026-08-24/memos/monotone-branch-fill-bench.md.
  multiforest-mutation-gaps: doors open
    (docs/plans/archive/multiforest-mutation-gaps.md):
    BCF whole-data setData (n free, z required): KEEP UNDESIGNED,
    gated on a considered failure to find an enabled model - every
    verified multi-forest class holds n fixed, and the BART
    adaptive-trial designs that exist cold-start per refresh.
    Per-forest row subsetting (mask vs physical compaction): value
    lifted by the AFT mixture-cure class (Sun & Song, whose authors
    reimplemented bcf's tree code standalone to get it -
    github roxiesun/TBAFTcure), shape UNRESOLVED (settle whether the
    subset forest wants its own cut grid first; the two interested
    classes may want different shapes). Design-gated, NOT scheduled
    (VD: revisit on a second consumer or a release want).
    monotoneTreeIsFeasible's 1e-9: deliberately left (it is the
    acceptance predicate of the constrained-prior rejection sampler,
    a one-sided feasibility slack, not an equality tolerance).
  negbin-real-dispersion: recorded door out of the negative-binomial
    landing (docs/plans/archive/negative-binomial.md; design sec 2 carries fork
    B's spec). Real-valued dispersion needs a non-integer-shape
    Polya-Gamma draw, for which no exact sampler exists, so shipping it
    means dbarts' first documented-approximate family (truncated
    gamma-sum, bias bounded ~1e-3 at K = 200) behind an explicit
    opt-in; the same decision gates weighted-binary's fractional
    weights. The engine seams are in place. Poisson family and grouped
    NB are companion doors (design sec 7). decision-gated.
  pre-review-cleanup: LANDED 7cd71f2d, see docs/plans/pre-review-cleanup.md.
    Open doors from its s5, not tracked elsewhere in TODO: the R-visible
    `cutpoints` spelling vs the engine/C-API `ordinalThresholds` rename
